This crate (`symphonia-codec-speex`) is a pure-Rust Speex audio decoder. It is licensed under the
Mozilla Public License, v. 2.0, like the rest of Project Symphonia (see `LICENSE`).

The decoder is ported, function-by-function, from the floating-point decoder of the reference
`libspeex` 1.2.1 implementation (https://github.com/xiph/speex): the narrow-band CELP decoder
(`nb_celp.c`), the sub-band CELP decoder (`sb_celp.c`), the intensity stereo expansion
(`stereo.c`), the LSP, LPC and filter helpers (`lsp.c`, `filters.c`, `ltp.c`, `lpc.c`,
`misc.c`, `math_approx.c`), the sub-mode descriptions (`modes.c`), the bit reader (`bits.c`), and
the header layout (`speex_header.c`). All the codebook tables (`tables.rs`) are extracted
programmatically from the `libspeex` tables (`gain_table*.c`, `lsp_tables_nb.c`,
`high_lsp_tables.c`, `exc_*_table.c`, `hexc*_table.c`, `quant_lsp.c`, `filters.c`). `libspeex` is
